  "prompt": "Which app events do LedgerLoop users land on? For each event_name, count the sessions whose first event has that name. Use every app event in the data. A user's first app event starts a session, and an event more than 30 minutes after the same user's previous event starts a new one; an event exactly 30 minutes later stays in the same session. Measure each gap as the time between the two moments in event_ts, a UTC instant, never between clock times. Return two columns, in this order: landing_event and sessions. Return one row for each event_name that starts at least one session. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "landing_event",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "sessions",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
